{"causes": ["The institutionalized system of the Roman Principate required the annual appointment of consuls to maintain administrative and ceremonial continuity.", "The ongoing political and social structures of the Roman Empire provided the framework for individuals like Gallus to ascend to high office.", "The reign of Emperor Nero necessitated the continuation of traditional Roman magistracies to legitimize imperial rule and manage the state."], "effects": ["Lucius Afinius Gallus's consulship contributed to the administrative stability and legal processes of the Roman Empire in 62 CE.", "His co-consulship with Publius Marius maintained the traditional collegial leadership structure of the highest Roman magistracy for the year.", "His tenure helped to reinforce the symbolic power of the consulship within the imperial system, even as its executive authority diminished under Nero."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "lucius-afinius-gallus", "sourceName": "Lucius Afinius Gallus", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "publius-marius", "targetName": "Publius Marius", "context": "Lucius Afinius Gallus served as co-consul with Publius Marius in 62 CE, sharing the highest civil magistracy of the Roman Empire."}, {"sourceSlug": "reign-of-nero", "sourceName": "Reign of Nero", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "lucius-afinius-gallus", "targetName": "Lucius Afinius Gallus", "context": "The political environment and imperial authority of Nero's reign significantly influenced the context and function of Lucius Afinius Gallus's consulship in 62 CE."}, {"sourceSlug": "lucius-afinius-gallus", "sourceName": "Lucius Afinius Gallus", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "roman-empire", "targetName": "Roman Empire", "context": "Lucius Afinius Gallus's entire known political career, including his consulship, occurred during the era of the Roman Empire."}, {"sourceSlug": "lucius-afinius-gallus", "sourceName": "Lucius Afinius Gallus", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "r